From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 17:56:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/9] test(records): read the split records engine where each
 part now lives
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Red at 917c70e (culprit 76f66a5d, PR #90):
  relations › the records engine renders the picker, the filter and the parent panel
  relations › an app with no parent still renders — the picker is simply absent
  relations › and an edit now reaches the server instead of only this browser
  an-export-that-exports-nothing › reads visible.length, which is what leaves with him
  an-export-that-exports-nothing › hands that same visible list to toCsv

Root cause: 76f66a5d split RecordsApp.jsx into src/app/records-controller.js
(state, storage, server), src/components/RecordsView.jsx (rendering) and a
RecordsApp.jsx that only mounts the view with the controller. The tests read
the wrapper, which holds none of it. Every buildAppFiles records path emits
all three modules; the static_records fallback refuses relation and API
blueprints (canBuildDependencyFreeRecordsApp), so no artifact mode drops the
picker or the server edit silently.

Decision: P. Each token is now read in the module that owns it, plus the
wiring (RecordsApp imports the controller and mounts RecordsView with it), so
a feature in a view nobody renders cannot pass. The NEGATIVE export case
("no longer reads rows.length") had been passing vacuously on the wrapper; it
reads the view again. "hands that same visible list" now checks the rows
argument of every toCsv call in the button, not "a visible within 400 chars".

Mutations (production file broken, restored, sha256 identical each time):
  rel1 drop onSubmit={addParent}      -> picker test ✕ Expected substring "onSubmit={addParent}"
  rel2 const rel = null               -> 2 ✕ Expected substring "const rel = content.relation"
  rel3 no apiUpdate on edit           -> ✕ Expected substring "apiUpdate(content.api, editing, patch)"
  rel4 wrapper returns null           -> 3 ✕ Expected substring "<RecordsView content={content} controller={controller} />"
  exp1 disabled={!rows.length}        -> 3 ✕ (visible.length / not rows.length / toCsv)
  exp2 non-parent branch toCsv(rows)  -> ✕ Expected /^visible\b/, Received "rows" (old check passed)
  exp3 wrapper returns null           -> 3 ✕ Expected the RecordsView mount

